> Are you saying this fixes #18051? 

It fixes it only for `@typescript-eslint/parser@4.x`. For any version below (or other parsers) this PR has no effect.

> Why?

Isn't #18051 similar to the test I added?

```jsx
function Foo({ Component }) {
  React.useEffect(() => {
    console.log(<Component />);
  }, [Component]);
};
```

I tried the added test with `@typescript-eslint/parser@3.x` and with that parser the code is (falsely) considered valid. I can restructure how the tests are partitioned so that it's more obvious that one test is invalid with one parser but valid with another one.

issue_context.body:
This seems to happen when
1. I take a component as a prop
2. I use that component as a JSX constructor in a hook

Minimal repro:
```jsx
export const Foo = ({ Component }) => {
  React.useEffect(() => {
    console.log(<Component />);
  }, []);
};
```

```
    "eslint-plugin-react-hooks": "^4.1.1",
```


---

Interestingly, this does NOT cause the error:
```jsx
export const Foo = ({ component }) => {
  React.useEffect(() => {
    const Component = component;
    console.log(<Component />);
  }, []);
};
```
